---
import EvidenceNote from '../components/EvidenceNote.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How The Haunted Archives distinguishes documented history, testimony, folklore, paranormal claims, and possible natural explanations."
>
  <header class="information-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Editorial methodology</p>
    <h1>Evidence stays in its proper category.</h1>
    <p class="information-hero__lead">
      The archive preserves uncertainty without blurring the line between the historical record
      and supernatural interpretation.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="information-section shell" aria-labelledby="distinctions-heading">
    <header class="information-section__heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Evidence framework</p>
      <h2 id="distinctions-heading">Five distinctions</h2>
    </header>

    <ol class="evidence-framework" role="list">
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><p>Documented history is presented as fact.</p></li>
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><p>Eyewitness accounts are treated as testimony.</p></li>
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><p>Folklore and urban legends are identified as such.</p></li>
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">04</span><p>Paranormal interpretations remain claims rather than conclusions.</p></li>
      <li><span aria-hidden="true">05</span><p>Natural explanations are considered as hypotheses with the same caution.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="methodology-caution shell" aria-labelledby="caution-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Limits of interpretation</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="caution-heading">Claims are not conclusions.</h2>
      <p>The archive does not rate supernatural claims as proven.</p>
      <p>Possible natural explanations are hypotheses subject to the same caution.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EvidenceNote />
</BaseLayout>
